{"id": "EUVD-2026-102358", "enisaUuid": "d9b99fb8-d353-305a-98dc-1c2e76f00ac6", "description": "catdoc through 0.95 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in copy_unicode_string() in src/xlsparse.c that allows attackers to read past buffers via an unchecked string character count. Attackers can supply a crafted .xls file declaring 0xFFFF two-byte characters in LABEL, STRING, or SST records to disclose adjacent memory through xls2csv output or crash the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:10:59", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/catdoc-xls-mulrk-endcol-and-string-count-oob-read", "https://github.com/vbwagner/catdoc/blob/38a2807d22ce1a08bc39b94e9072a9f8f52cd86f/src/xlsparse.c#L421-L520", "https://github.com/vbwagner/catdoc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/catdoc-through-0.95-out-of-bounds-read-via-xls2csv-copy-unicode-string"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111127", "GHSA-f7rh-84jf-2xrr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9d4f387f-7524-38fd-9d09-a7c96b364f96", "product": {"name": "catdoc", "vendor": {"name": "catdoc"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.95"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1787cf32-cb4e-372f-938d-0591deffb9e4", "vendor": {"name": "catdoc"}}], "isExploited": false}